{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>It is double the wage of a hired worker; your slave has served you six years.</b> The term of hire, for it is not the custom among people to hire themselves out for a period longer than this, is three years, as it is written (Isaiah 16:14): ״שלש שנים כשני שכיר״ — 'three years, like the years of a hired worker.' And our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded from here that a Hebrew slave serves his master by day and by night, for his master assigns him a Canaanite maidservant for bearing children, and this is 'double the wage of a hired worker,' for the labor of a hired worker is only by day."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:48:28.033372249Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}